<title>USA: USDA declares Iowa cattle free of brucellosis.</title>
<headline>USDA declares Iowa cattle free of brucellosis.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department said Friday that Iowa now meets the standards for class-free status of brucellosis.</p>
<p>In a Federal Register notice, USDA said it was changing Iowa's classification to remove certain restrictions on the interstate movement of cattle.</p>
<p>The interim rule became effective on Tuesday, and the USDA will accept public comments on the change through Sept. 16.</p>
<p>Brucellosis is a contagious bacteria causing disease in animals and humans. States are classified according to the rate of brucella infection, and the class-free ranking based on a finding of no known brucellosis in cattle for 12 months.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
